#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:4
msgid "# Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:7
msgid ""
"To configure **Tanglet**, open the **Settings** menu. You see the following "
"entries:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Show Maximum Score** – you can choose between three options for the "
"status\n"
"line at the bottom of the window:  \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:12
msgid "![Listed maximum scores](./figures/tanglet_toggle_maximum_score_display.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#: ../configuration.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Never** – You see word lengths and the count of words found for each "
"length."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   * **End Of Game** – At the end of the game, you see the contained words "
"per\n"
"    word length and the count of words found by you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#: ../configuration.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Always**: The behavior described for **End Of Game** is always visible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:22
msgid ""
"The visibility of the word count status bar can be toggled with **Show Word "
"Counts**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:24
msgid "![Word count status](./figures/tanglet_word_counts.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Show Missed Words** – In addition to the list of found words on the "
"left, an\n"
"extra tab named **Missed** will de displayed. This tab is inactive until "
"the\n"
"game ends.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:32
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Board Language** – You can change the board language by clicking on "
"the\n"
"drop-down list and choose from the available languages. Besides that, you "
"have\n"
"some extra options:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:34
msgid "![Language settings](./figures/tanglet_board_language.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:42
msgid ""
"You can change the file paths to **Dice**, **Word List** and **Dictionary** "
"by entering the file paths manually or click on the respective **Choose…** "
"buttons to open a file chooser dialog. To set all entries back to the "
"defaults, click on **Defaults** in the bottom left corner of the window.  As "
"usual, you can stop editing the preferences with the **Cancel** button, and "
"apply the changes with **OK**. Your changes will be applied after the next "
"start of **Tanglet**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:47
msgid ""
"Under **Application Language**, you can change the language of the user "
"interface. The settings window opens with the button **System language**.  "
"Click on it to change the desired language from the drop-down menu. Again, "
"your changes will be applied after the next start of **Tanglet**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:59
msgid ""
"<!-- This is my workaround for taking the English screenshots --> > [!NOTE] "
"> Not all translated captions come from **Tanglet** itself. Because some of "
"> them are provided by the underlying **Qt** libraries, it might happen that "
"> some captions are still displayed in the system language. Maybe the "
"following > command is known to you for opening an application with "
"different language > settings: > > `$ export LC_ALL=C && tanglet` > > This "
"helps in such cases to switch completely to the desired language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../configuration.md:60 ../contributing.md:40 ../credits.md:16 ../files.md:54
#: ../howtoplay.md:79 ../menubar.md:57
msgid "[Back to the index page](./index.md)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:4
msgid "# Contributing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"The **Tanglet** development is maintained in a [Github "
"repository](https://github.com/gottcode/tanglet/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:9
msgid "## Contributing with code"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:12
msgid ""
"If you have a Github account, feel free to fork the project, apply and "
"commit your changes and open a Pull Request. This is the preferred way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:14
msgid "## Issue tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:22
msgid ""
"You found a bug, like to request a new feature or have any other suggestion? "
"Please got to [our issue "
"tracker](https://github.com/gottcode/tanglet/issues)  and open a new one by "
"clicking on **New issue** in the top right corner of the page. This also "
"applies for the documentation, if parts are confusing or missing, or for "
"wrong translations. Regarding incomplete translations: Don't treat it as a "
"bug worth to be filed. Our translators don't always have as much time as "
"needed, so translations may be incomplete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:24
msgid "## Translations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Tanglet** is available in various languages. The appropriate `.ts` and "
"`.po`\n"
"files are maintained at\n"
"[Transifex](https://explore.transifex.com/gottcode/tanglet/). If you like "
"to\n"
"contribute to translations, register or sign in there, join a translation "
"team\n"
"or create a new one for your desired language, if needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:34
msgid ""
"For the translations itself, Transifex offers a web-based editor. If you "
"prefer to work on the files directly, you can also download and edit them "
"locally in your preferred tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../contributing.md:39
msgid ""
"Although **Tanglet** is not part of any integrated desktop environment, "
"please always try to follow the basic rules of well-known translation teams "
"for your language, for example, those of the "
"[KDE](https://l10n.kde.org/teams-list.php)  or "
"[GNOME](https://l10n.gnome.org/teams/) teams."
msgstr ""

