#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:4
msgid "# Menu Bar Overview"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:6
msgid "## Game menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **New Game** – Starts a new game. If a previous game is still running, "
"you\n"
"will asked for confirmation to stop that game.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **New Roll** – Starts a new game in the same mode as the currently "
"running\n"
"one. Again, you will asked for confirmation to stop that game.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Choose…** – Lets you start a game which has been saved previously. A "
"file\n"
"chooser dialog will be opened where you can search for the desired game "
"file.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Share…** – Lets you save the game in a file. A file chooser dialog will "
"be\n"
"opened where you can choose for a file name and directory. Although it is\n"
"possible, keep the **File type** entry unchanged. We don't recommend to "
"save\n"
"files with another extension than `.tanglet`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: ../menubar.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**End** – End the game. You will asked for confirmation to stop the game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Pause** – Pause the game. Probably you need this for time-limited "
"games.\n"
"When pausing a game, the whole window content disappears. After clicking\n"
"anywhere in the window, the pause ends and the content comes back. Note, "
"also\n"
"when the window losts the focus, the window content disappears.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Details** – Shows details about the running game, such as the board "
"size,\n"
"the word density and length, the game type and a short description of that "
"game.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **High Scores** – Shows the High Scores. The initial view shows the High\n"
"Scores for the type of the currently running game. To view the High Scores\n"
"for the other game types, click on the vertical tab bar on the left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: ../menubar.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Quit** – Quits the game and the application."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:38
msgid "## Settings menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:41
msgid ""
"See [Configuration](./configuration.md) about how to use the entries of the "
"**Settings** menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:43
msgid "## Help menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Controls** – Shows a brief summary of the usage. In fact, the same as\n"
"described in the [How to Play](./howtoplay.md) page.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **User manual** – Opens this user manual in your configured standard "
"browser.\n"
"The opened application is out of the scope of **Tanglet**; if you like to "
"use a\n"
"different browser or HTML viewer, you need to configure this in the settings "
"of\n"
"your desktop environment.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: ../menubar.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**About** – Shows a brief summary, including the version number of "
"**Tanglet**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../menubar.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **About Qt** – Shows a description of [Qt](https://www.qt.io/), which is "
"the\n"
"code base of **Tanglet**.\n"
msgstr ""
